# Verum FP-regression corpus manifest.
#
# Each non-comment, non-blank line is one repository:
#
#   name  group  sha  url
#
# - name  : short identifier, used as the key in snapshot.json (must be unique)
# - group : one of rust | web | parsers | network (loose language/domain tag,
#           used only to group results in reports - it has no effect on the run)
# - sha   : commit SHA the repo is pinned to. Findings are only comparable
#           run-to-run if the input tree is byte-identical, so every entry
#           MUST be pinned - never a branch name or tag that can move.
# - url   : git remote to fetch the SHA from (must support fetching a
#           specific commit, e.g. GitHub, GitLab; see corpus/run.py)
#
# To bump a pin: resolve the new SHA (e.g. `git ls-remote <url> <ref>`),
# update the line below, then regenerate the baseline - see corpus/README.md.

